{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790624880,"nonce":"0qyQaRT12bA6fqOzr8CF7192PEI=","message":"Landed 2026-09-28 (Luis, with Claude): the board draws in the terminal, so this task is done; gantt and nesting are 565d57a under the gantt story (00a63d9).\n\nCalls made while planning it, recorded in doc/design/terminal-renderer.md, Board:\n\n- Enter opens the card in show; nothing on a card is edited in place. The only edits a board makes are moves, because a card is a summary and the page with the field on it is where a field is edited. This supersedes the older \"ask which field on a card\". Copy in every spelling copies the id; a paste has nowhere to go.\n- Grab needs no rank: Space always grabs, ←/→ carry the card into the neighbouring column (empty or not) and the drop sets the columns field (null in (none)); ↑/↓ need rank and say so without it. One drop is one set with up to two keys, so one commit; a card dropped where it was picked up writes nothing; a drop the schema refuses is a status line and nothing else; a refresh while grabbed lets the card go.\n- Columns: values when given, else the field's schema order read off the types the cards on the board have (an iteration's statuses are not columns of a board of tasks — found by a test against the jira preset), then the values the data has that are not listed, then (none). Listed columns are drawn empty; trailing ones only while a card is in them.\n- A card is the short id, the title wrapped to the column, then each other card field as key: value on its own line; the cursor card washed with its id reversed, as a list row.\n- Columns keep a minimum width of 20 and the board scrolls sideways by whole columns to follow the cursor; ‹ › on the header say there is more. Lanes (group_by) scroll as one canvas so they stay aligned.\n\nCode: tui/board.go (the page), tui/board_view.go (the drawing), tui/board_test.go; lessByRank and scroll lifted